cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ToolDiscoveryBench, please cite it as below."
title: "ToolDiscoveryBench: benchmarking routers that pick the right MCP tool"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bellam
    given-names: Sarath Chandra
repository-code: "https://github.com/SarathChandraBellam/ToolDiscoveryBench"
url: "https://github.com/SarathChandraBellam/ToolDiscoveryBench"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for the tool-search step of AI agents: given a request and a catalog of real
  MCP tools, which tool should be called first, or none? It compares BM25, embeddings and
  decision models (TypeSafe Jev, GPT-6 Luna Decisions) against first-tool picks from the
  Claude Code and Codex agent harnesses, reporting accuracy, abstention, latency, cost and
  calibration.
keywords:
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - tool-retrieval
  - tool-calling
  - benchmark
  - agents
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
